/Title (Educational policies significantly influence teaching effectiveness and student achievement because they shape curriculum implementation, classroom assessment, and instructional practices. Recent reforms by the Department of Education emphasize authentic learning and stronger accountability in assessing student performance rather than relying solely on adjusted grading systems. These policy changes suggest that well-designed educational reforms can enhance students' academic performance when effectively implemented at the school level)
