/Title (The main goal of this study is to determine the effect of remittance frequency on the financial planning behavior of Overseas Filipino Workers \(OFWs\). Specifically, it aims to examine whether the frequency of sending remittances influences how OFWs and their families manage budgeting, saving, investing, and other financial planning practices. The findings of the study are expected to provide insights into the relationship between remittance patterns and financial management, which may help families, financial institutions, and policymakers develop strategies to promote better financial planning among OFWs.)
